# Update / deploy

When the user says **update**, **deploy**, or equivalent (ship, publish, push live):

## 1. Make the page work

- Finish the feature/fix; do not leave broken UI.
- Run `npm test` and `npx tsc --noEmit` (or `npm run build` with `GITHUB_PAGES=true` if deploy-shaped).
- Spot-check critical flows in the browser when UI changed (settings, search, chart list).

## 2. Version + changelog

- Bump `package.json` patch version (e.g. 1.4.12 → 1.4.13).
- Add a matching entry at the top of `lib/changelog-data.json` with short user-facing notes.
- Rebuild so `public/app-version.json` / `public/changelog.json` match (or whatever the project’s version write step is).

## 3. Commit and push GitHub `main`

- Commit only when shipping (user asked update/deploy).
- Push to **`github` remote `main`** (`https://github.com/charles-lhyu/Dominos-stock-shelf-life.git`) — that triggers Pages.
- Do not stop at Cursor Origin alone; GitHub `main` is what deploys.

## 4. Confirm deployment and live page

- Watch the **Deploy GitHub Pages** workflow until success (`gh run watch` / `gh run list`).
- Confirm Pages status built and URL: https://charles-lhyu.github.io/Dominos-stock-shelf-life/
- Hard-check the live site (version label / `app-version.json` matches the shipped version).
- Report commit, workflow result, and live URL/version to the user.

## Do not

- Push a known failing build.
- Skip the live confirmation step after push.
